msgid "Zero-noise extrapolation with probabilistic error amplification for the latest version of Qiskit mitigation"
msgstr "Zero-noise extrapolation na may probabilistic error amplification para sa pinakabagong bersyon ng Qiskit mitigation"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: title
#, no-wrap
msgid "Zero-noise extrapolation with probabilistic error amplification"
msgstr "Zero-noise extrapolation na may probabilistic error amplification"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<OpenInLabBanner notebookPath=\"addons/qiskit-mitigation/guides/pea-with-noise-learning.ipynb\" />\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Zero-noise extrapolation (ZNE) is a technique for mitigating quantum noise in observable expectation value calculations. It works by executing a quantum circuit at increasing noise scales, taking expectation values with respect to those noise scales, and extrapolating to estimate a zero-noise expectation value. Both the noise amplification and extrapolation stages can be implemented in different ways. In this guide you will amplify the noise with probabilistic error amplification (PEA), as suggested in [\"Evidence for the utility of quantum computing before fault tolerance\"](https://www.nature.com/articles/s41586-023-06096-3). To amplify with PEA, you must first model the noise affecting the circuit's entangling gates.  You can also implement amplification with digital gate folding, which needs no noise model and is covered in the [gate folding guide](/addons/qiskit-mitigation/guides/gate-folding-with-custom-extrapolation). You will learn the noise with [``qiskit-noise-learning``](https://github.com/Qiskit/qiskit-noise-learning) and extrapolate with the built-in exponential fitting strategy.\n"
msgstr "Ang zero-noise extrapolation (ZNE) ay isang teknik para bawasan ang quantum noise sa mga kalkulasyon ng expectation value ng observable. Gumagana ito sa pamamagitan ng pagpapatakbo ng quantum circuit sa tumataas na noise scale, pagkuha ng mga expectation value ayon sa mga noise scale na iyon, at pag-extrapolate para tantiyahin ang zero-noise expectation value. Parehong maipapatupad sa iba't ibang paraan ang mga yugto ng noise amplification at extrapolation. Sa gabay na ito, ia-amplify mo ang noise gamit ang probabilistic error amplification (PEA), gaya ng iminungkahi sa [\"Evidence for the utility of quantum computing before fault tolerance\"](https://www.nature.com/articles/s41586-023-06096-3). Para mag-amplify gamit ang PEA, kailangan mo munang i-model ang noise na nakakaapekto sa mga entangling gate ng circuit.  Maaari mo ring ipatupad ang amplification gamit ang digital gate folding, na hindi nangangailangan ng noise model at tinatalakay sa [gate folding guide](/addons/qiskit-mitigation/guides/gate-folding-with-custom-extrapolation). Aaralin mo ang noise gamit ang [``qiskit-noise-learning``](https://github.com/Qiskit/qiskit-noise-learning) at mag-e-extrapolate ka gamit ang built-in na exponential fitting strategy.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Keep in mind, while ZNE can be effective at mitigating quantum noise for a lower sampling cost than other methods, it comes with no bounds on the bias.\n"
msgstr "Tandaan, bagama't epektibo ang ZNE sa pagbabawas ng quantum noise sa mas mababang sampling cost kaysa sa ibang paraan, wala itong anumang hangganan sa bias.\n"

