# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Learn the noise of the entangling layers with `qiskit-noise-learning` {#learn-the-noise-of-the-entangling-layers-with-qiskit-noise-learning}"
msgstr "Alamin ang noise ng mga entangling layer gamit ang `qiskit-noise-learning` {#learn-the-noise-of-the-entangling-layers-with-qiskit-noise-learning}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "PEA starts by learning the twirled noise model of each layer of entangling gates in the circuit. We assume a Markovian noise model, and therefore only the noise model of each unique layer of entangling gates should be learned, because the depth of the circuit is assumed to not affect the noise channel of a given entangling layer. The more accurate the learned noise model is, the more accurate the amplification will be.\n"
msgstr "Nagsisimula ang PEA sa pag-aaral ng twirled noise model ng bawat layer ng entangling gates sa circuit. Ipinapalagay natin ang Markovian na noise model, kaya ang noise model lang ng bawat natatanging layer ng entangling gates ang kailangang matutunan, dahil ipinapalagay na hindi naaapektuhan ng depth ng circuit ang noise channel ng isang entangling layer. Kung mas tumpak ang natutunang noise model, mas tumpak din ang amplification.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We use `qiskit-noise-learning` for learning the noise. The learner repeats each layer `fragment_depths` times in its learning circuits, twirls each circuit `num_randomizations` times, and fits the decay of the measured fidelities to a Pauli-Lindblad model. The following code draws the learned noise model, with the two layers merged into one map. Each qubit is a pie of its weight-1 X, Y, and Z rates summed over the two layers, and each edge shows the learned weight-2 rates; a rate of ``3e-4`` means that error occurs on roughly three of every 10,000 uses of the layer.\n"
msgstr "Ginagamit natin ang `qiskit-noise-learning` para matutunan ang noise. Inuulit ng learner ang bawat layer nang `fragment_depths` beses sa mga learning circuit nito, nagta-twirl ng bawat circuit nang `num_randomizations` beses, at ifi-fit ang pagbaba ng mga nasukat na fidelity sa isang Pauli-Lindblad model. Ipinapakita ng sumusunod na code ang natutunang noise model, kung saan pinagsama sa isang mapa ang dalawang layer. Ang bawat qubit ay isang pie ng weight-1 na X, Y, at Z rate nito na pinagsama sa dalawang layer, at ipinapakita ng bawat edge ang mga natutunang weight-2 rate; ang rate na ``3e-4`` ay nangangahulugang nagaganap ang error na iyon sa humigit-kumulang tatlo sa bawat 10,000 gamit ng layer.\n"

