# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Prepare a ZNE program with probabilistic error amplification and sample circuits of varying noise scales {#prepare-a-zne-program-with-probabilistic-error-amplification-and-sample-circuits-of-varying-noise-scales}"
msgstr "Maghanda ng ZNE program na may probabilistic error amplification at mag-sample ng mga circuit na may iba't ibang noise scale {#prepare-a-zne-program-with-probabilistic-error-amplification-and-sample-circuits-of-varying-noise-scales}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Here you will prepare a ZNE program containing circuits of increasing noise scales. With PEA, each noise factor represents the multiple of the learned noise the circuit experiences: a noise factor of ``2.0`` injects one additional copy of each layer's learned noise channel after that layer, on top of the noise the layer already has. Because PEA scales the learned noise rates directly rather than repeating gates, any noise factor is possible, including non-integer ones, and the circuit itself is not modified: the program items share one template circuit and differ only in the noise injected by the samplex. The injected noise is sampled once per randomization, so the statistical error of PEA is controlled by the number of randomizations rather than the shots per randomization; we therefore use many randomizations with a few shots each, keeping the total number of shots the same as for the unmitigated program. It is important to not use too few randomizations, as otherwise you might encounter sampling bias in the noise injection.\n"
msgstr "Dito, maghahanda ka ng ZNE program na naglalaman ng mga circuit na may pataas na noise scale. Sa PEA, ang bawat noise factor ay kumakatawan sa multiple ng natutunang noise na nararanasan ng circuit: ang noise factor na ``2.0`` ay nag-i-inject ng isa pang kopya ng natutunang noise channel ng bawat layer pagkatapos ng layer na iyon, bukod pa sa noise na mayroon na ang layer. Dahil direktang ini-scale ng PEA ang mga natutunang noise rate sa halip na ulitin ang mga gate, posible ang anumang noise factor, kasama ang mga hindi integer, at hindi binabago ang circuit mismo: iisang template circuit ang ginagamit ng mga item ng programa at magkakaiba lang sila sa noise na ini-inject ng samplex. Isang beses sa bawat randomization sina-sample ang ini-inject na noise, kaya ang statistical error ng PEA ay kinokontrol ng bilang ng mga randomization sa halip na ng mga shot bawat randomization; kaya gumagamit tayo ng maraming randomization na may kaunting shot bawat isa, habang pinananatiling pareho ang kabuuang bilang ng shot sa unmitigated na programa. Mahalagang huwag gumamit ng masyadong kaunting randomization, dahil kung hindi, maaari kang makaranas ng sampling bias sa noise injection.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The total sampling overhead scales linearly with the number of noise factors.\n"
msgstr "Ang kabuuang sampling overhead ay linear na tumataas kasabay ng bilang ng mga noise factor.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Finally, run the program on the noisy simulator. Its results feed the extrapolation in the next step.\n"
msgstr "Panghuli, patakbuhin ang programa sa noisy na simulator. Ang mga resulta nito ang gagamitin sa extrapolation sa susunod na hakbang.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Extrapolate to the zero-noise limit {#extrapolate-to-the-zero-noise-limit}"
msgstr "I-extrapolate sa zero-noise limit {#extrapolate-to-the-zero-noise-limit}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Now that you have data for each noise scale, you can fit a function to the data and extrapolate back to the zero-noise value to estimate an expectation value of the noise-free observable. Under Pauli noise an observable decays exponentially with the noise factor, so you will choose the exponential extrapolator as your first choice, and fall back to the linear one if the exponential fit fails. To visualize the extrapolation, plot the site-averaged magnetization calculated at each noise factor, the exponential fit, and the site average of the extrapolated expectation values at the zero-noise point. We see the fit slightly undershoots for this particular observable.\n"
msgstr "Ngayong mayroon ka nang data para sa bawat noise scale, maaari kang mag-fit ng function sa data at mag-extrapolate pabalik sa zero-noise value para tantiyahin ang expectation value ng noise-free na observable. Sa ilalim ng Pauli noise, exponential na bumababa ang observable kasabay ng noise factor, kaya ang exponential extrapolator ang pipiliin mo bilang unang pagpipilian, at babalik sa linear kung pumalya ang exponential fit. Para i-visualize ang extrapolation, i-plot ang site-averaged na magnetization na kinalkula sa bawat noise factor, ang exponential fit, at ang site average ng mga na-extrapolate na expectation value sa zero-noise point. Makikita natin na bahagyang kulang ang fit para sa partikular na observable na ito.\n"

